silm:instances_papers_25_sheaf_gluing_chapters_01_sheaf_basics_local_sections_sections_02_presheaf_of_typed_sections_concrete_anchor_4#vetowneroverlap1sectionset a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.25_sheaf_gluing.chapters.01_sheaf_basics_local_sections.sections.02_presheaf_of_typed_sections.concrete_anchor_4#vetowneroverlap1sectionset" .
silm:instances_papers_25_sheaf_gluing_chapters_01_sheaf_basics_local_sections_sections_02_presheaf_of_typed_sections_concrete_anchor_4#vetowneroverlap1sectionset silm:hasLongDescription "The VetOwnerOverlap1SectionSet is the small set of facts known during the half-day overlap that BOTH the vet and the owner must agree on (microchip ID, body-mass quality, household role). In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'F_Mittens(U_{vet1} cap U_{owner1})', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
